WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.470
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.380
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:21.130
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.830
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.930
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.300
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.230
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.480
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.750
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:03.490
What is truly precious?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.380
Take this!  Dark Mega Flare!

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:19.220
No way!  How can I lose to that kid?

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.030
Jonouchi is the winner!

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:25.400
I did it!

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:33.940
After a brief recess, we'll begin the tournament's final match between Yugi Muto and Katsuya Jonouchi.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.780
The time has finally come, Yugi.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:47.490
Finals of Friendship!
Yugi vs Jonouchi (Part 1)

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.860
Let's begin the tournament's final match.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.430
In the final match, Yugi Muto will face Katsuya Jonouchi.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.370
Grandpa!

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.380
Yugi, we believe in you.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:15.380
We know you'll save us.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.260
Bye bye, Jonouchi.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.260
Wipe your nose.  You look pathetic.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:32.860
I never expected that Duelist Kingdom's final match would be Yugi vs Jonouchi.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.580
Yeah.  But a battle is a battle.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.270
They'll battle with all their strength.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.980
But why?

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:43.480
Even if Yugi wins, he'll give the prize money to Jonouchi.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.280
So why do they have to fight?

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.150
Without a winner, no one gets the prize money.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.180
I understand that.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.520
But those two are best friends.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.720
They shouldn't seriously fight each other!

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.140
They're fighting because they are friends.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.740
That's true friendship.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.730
That doesn't make any sense!

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.100
Jonouchi...

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:08.430
Yugi, don't you dare say that you can't duel me.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.530
Well?

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.400
I knew we'd eventually have to fight, but when the moment actually arrives...

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.080
Battle me, Yugi!

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:22.150
We each have our own reasons for battling to the end, and that's what we decided to do!

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:28.580
We both got here because we decided to win to the end, no matter who the opponent was!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.650
Am I wrong?

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.660
Jonouchi is right.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:37.660
We both must battle to the end for our own reasons.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.260
Will you accept this battle against me?

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.740
Fine, Jonouchi.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.450
Yugi...

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.200
You've both done well for making it this far.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:06.420
As the organizer of Duelist Kingdom, I greatly commend you.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.660
Battle with all your might so that you won't be left with regrets.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.500
Yugi, before this duel begins, I have to thank you.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:26.540
Can you believe I'm actually facing you in the final match?

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.280
I couldn't have made it this far without you and the others.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.780
Jonouchi.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:39.720
I finally understand that I wanted to duel you for real.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.780
There's an incredible power hidden within you.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:49.230
By battling you, I want some of that power to rub off on me.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.840
Let's do this, Yugi!

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:57.470
Jonouchi's duelist instincts are trying to awaken.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.460
His instincts to challenge someone stronger than himself.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.720
This will be interesting.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:13.920
They're bound by deep friendship, but they're willing to lay all their strength to determine who's superior.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.700
I sense that this will be an incredible final match.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:21.700
Jonouchi, I won't hold back.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:22.920
I'll use all my strength!

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:26.920
Yugi, I'll strike you with all my power.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.740
That's my proof that we're friends.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.610
Start the duel!

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:42.220
Duel!

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.590
I'll go first!

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:46.560
Bring it!

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.560
Celtic Guardian in attack position!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:06:00.840
Both Yugi and Jonouchi have the same goal: to help someone dear to them.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.080
So why...

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.640
That has nothing to do with what's happening here.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:08.900
Right now, they're duelists that want to have the best battle possible.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.650
That's all they're thinking.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:12.480
That's what being a man is all about.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:19.160
But I'm not sure if Jonouchi's attack pattern that relies on strength will work against Yugi.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:23.760
What a pure and beautiful sight.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:29.730
Two beasts have been released into the arena known as the Duel Ring.

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:32.040
It's your turn, Jonouchi!

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.870
Here I go, Yugi!

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:38.270
I summon Giltia the D. Knight in attack position!

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:45.700
Battle!

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.120
Magic attack with Soul Spear!

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.530
Celtic Guardian is destroyed!

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.940
What's wrong, Yugi?

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.570
Bring out something that's more of a challenge!

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:14.720
Jonouchi is suddenly full of confidence.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:17.520
But this duel has just begun.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:22.980
When it comes to composure, Yugi is several steps ahead of Jonouchi.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:24.090
What do you mean?

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.140
Look at Yugi's eyes.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:32.600
They're burning with fighting spirit, but they're also analyzing Jonouchi's moves.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:38.420
In the past, Jonouchi would've kept relying on power.

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.870
But Jonouchi has changed.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:46.540
After passing many trials, he can now think strategically.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.650
I need to be careful.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.150
Jonouchi!

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:54.520
What?

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:59.920
In this game, monster battles carry risks.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:07.640
If I bring out a monster with greater attack points, it'll always defeat yours if they battle.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:12.530
Yeah.  I've learned that since coming to this island.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:14.570
I understand fully.

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:20.240
The balance between spell cards and monster cards forms the foundation of Duel Monsters.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:24.220
Only those who master that can win.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:28.180
I've learned that from your duels, Yugi.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:33.300
Be careful that you don't foolishly use up your monster cards.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:37.190
Yeah.  Thanks for the advice.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:38.690
My turn!

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:43.100
Gaia the Fierce Knight in attack position!

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:45.730
Battle!

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.850
Giltia the D. Knight is destroyed!

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.500
That's the spirit, Yugi!

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.850
But I've changed from how I used to be!

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:07.320
Armored Lizard in defense position!

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:13.640
He's trying to get me to attack by playing a sacrificial pawn.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.000
Fine.  Let's see what you have in mind.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.500
What's wrong with Jonouchi?

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:23.280
No, Jonouchi has a plan.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.600
I see.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:31.810
What's wrong, Yugi?  It's your turn.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:33.320
Yeah.  Here I go!

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:36.030
Summoned Skull in attack position!

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.020
All right!

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:41.590
Magic Lightning!

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.930
Armored Lizard is destroyed!

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.460
Just like I thought.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.040
This is Jonouchi's strategy.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.040
No way.  He simply lost his monster.

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:02.600
No.  He has something planned.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:08.280
Since he's facing Yugi, Jonouchi would want to keep cards in his hand.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:16.290
But he played Armored Lizard even though he knew his opponent would play a stronger monster.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:18.330
Jonouchi...

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:23.820
I knew you would play that next.

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:29.480
I've been waiting for you to play Summoned Skull.

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:34.840
Yugi, you said the balance between spell cards and monster cards was important.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.980
I'm giving that same advice back to you!

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:09.080
My turn!

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:12.360
Flame Swordsman in attack position!

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:17.020
What's the meaning of this, Jonouchi?

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:20.340
What's he thinking?

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.740
It doesn't have enough attack points to win.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.320
But look at that.

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:27.230
I'll also use this.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:31.120
The spell card Shield & Sword.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.000
What?

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:35.240
Ah, you're playing that card now?

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:41.240
That spell card switches every monster's attack and defense points.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:42.610
That means...

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:57.500
My monster's attack points drop to 1600, but your monster's attack points drop to 1200.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:58.860
Battle!

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:02.440
Here I go!  Flaming Battle Sword!

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:11.170
Summoned Skull is destroyed!

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:16.510
Like I thought, Armored Lizard was a decoy to lure my Summoned Skull to the field.

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:22.250
Yugi, I can only defeat you by destroying your powerful monsters one at a time.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:26.560
You've improved a lot, Jonouchi.

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:30.540
Your spell-monster combo was impressive.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.490
Thanks for your praise.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.920
Jonouchi really is strong.

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.920
Yeah.  He's improved much more than I expected.

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:41.870
If Yugi isn't careful, he might lose.

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:44.240
Yugi...

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:51.480
Since they know each other's decks, strategy will play a big role.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:54.210
This is worth watching.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.950
Battle me for real, Yugi!

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:00.690
I have been, Jonouchi!

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:02.850
Then bring it on!

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:04.450
It's your turn!

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:05.690
Fine!

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.200
It's my turn!

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:11.820
Curse of Dragon in attack position!

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:24.650
Then I'll use Polymerization to fuse Curse of Dragon and Gaia the Fierce Knight.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:25.380
What?

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.820
Gaia the Dragon Champion!

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:40.530
Gaia the Dragon Champion attacks!

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.570
Flame Swordsman is destroyed!

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:53.440
Yugi.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:55.340
That was an overwhelming attack.

00:13:55.640 --> 00:14:03.920
Yugi has been calmly observing Jonouchi's moves, but he's now getting serious.

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:08.020
Jonouchi wouldn't like it if Yugi was going easy on him.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:10.170
That's not what I mean.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:15.160
They're instinctively fighting each other like two wild animals.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:20.000
Or else, he wouldn't have unleashed such an overwhelming attack.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.500
Because he only needs to do just enough win.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:23.960
No way...

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:28.010
It's Yugi and Jonouchi that are battling over there.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:32.700
Why do they have to battle each other so fiercely?

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:38.280
Because that's what it means to be a duelist.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:43.280
You are correct.

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:48.020
Once you enter the Ring, you must battle until you crush your opponent, no matter who it is.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:50.100
That is the world of dueling.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.700
This duel will become an intense fight.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:58.070
And no one can stop them anymore.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:03.280
What will you do, Jonouchi?

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:06.150
Try to defeat my Gaia the Dragon Champion!

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:09.150
Pull yourself together, Katsuya Jonouchi.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:11.650
Now's the time to give it your all.

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:16.640
Just focus on defeating Gaia the Dragon Champion.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.990
What happens afterwards isn't important.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:23.630
Gaia the Dragon Champion has 2600 attack points.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:30.140
The most powerful monster I have, Red-Eyes B. Dragon, has 2400 attack points.

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:34.840
But if I lose it, I have little chance of defeating Yugi.

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:42.060
Moments like this make dueling so exciting.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:48.970
Jonouchi boy is risking all his strength to destroy Yugi boy's Gaia the Dragon Champion.

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:54.130
But he won't be able to pull it off unless he has tremendous skill.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.630
What strategy will he think of?

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:04.700
A straightforward attack means I'll die in vain.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:12.110
I need to combo Red-Eyes with a spell card to make it more powerful than Gaia the Dragon Champion.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.110
But is there a way to do that?

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:24.890
Sorry, Jonouchi.  Since I've stepped into the Ring, I can't afford to lose.

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:28.910
I'll use everything at my disposal to stop your attack.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:31.540
What will you try next?

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.370
What should I do?

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.340
What should I do?

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:50.440
Copycat.

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:53.650
I see!  Copy!

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:56.890
And I have Graverobber in my hand!

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:03.880
If I use these two cards correctly, I can defeat Gaia the Dragon Champion and its 2600 attack points.

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:08.130
Did he create a strategy?

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:13.200
Yugi, I might be a genius.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:17.510
Your Gaia the Dragon Champion is finished!

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:18.810
What?

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:21.550
Jonouchi is about to make his move.

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:27.140
I summon Red-Eyes B. Dragon in attack position!

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:37.710
Then I use Graverobber to steal one card from your graveyard!

00:17:37.710 --> 00:17:38.760
What?

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:44.140
I'm taking your Summoned Skull!

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:46.720
No way!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.340
Yugi, I'll use the same tactic you did.

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:54.650
Next, I play Copycat!

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:58.130
It copies one card on your field.

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:02.120
It's too late to be surprised.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:06.430
The card I'm copying is Polymerization!

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:07.940
Polymerization?

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.040
That's right.

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:13.630
It'll be the first time I use it, but I know its effect is incredible.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:19.140
I fuse Summoned Skull and Red-Eyes B. Dragon!

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:38.060
The fiend dragon B. Skull Dragon!

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:39.120
What?

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:45.460
Beautiful!  Wonderful!  Terrific!

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:56.570
B. Skull Dragon, destroy Gaia the Dragon Champion!

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.380
Meteor Flare!

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:11.920
I did it!  Gaia the Dragon Champion is destroyed!

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:22.900
I warned you that I'll take your monsters down one at a time.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:36.320
Yugi, I'm finally starting to understand the thrill of dueling.

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:41.790
You're right.  This is a true duel, Jonouchi!

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:48.490
Where is this duel heading?

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:51.180
Only those two know.

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:55.360
There will be more twists and turns, but eventually...

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:56.220
What?

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:59.370
They will battle until one falls.

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:01.710
That's for certain.

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:04.480
Yugi...  Jonouchi...

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:11.480
I cannot take my eyes off this match.

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:15.370
The battle is only getting started!

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:16.800
Bring it on, Yugi!

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:19.480
Yeah!  Here I go, Jonouchi!

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:37.940
How can they fight each other with such intensity?

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:45.940
While watching Yugi and Jonouchi's breathtaking battle, I'm starting to understand how they feel.

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:50.570
Yugi and Jonouchi, no matter who wins, battle hard so that you won't have regrets later!

00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:55.030
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Finals of Friendship!
Yugi vs Jonouchi (Part 2)

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:57.020
Duel, standby!

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:11.050
The flask glistens

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:18.900
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:19.390 --> 00:21:27.880
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:35.650
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:41.480
Shower of happiness

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:45.590
I will shower you with it

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:53.870
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:58.100
Shower of happiness

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:02.230
You are not alone

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:08.950
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
